TIMESYNC(8)

NAME
    timesync - keep the kernel wall clock synchronized with SNTP

DESCRIPTION
    timesync sends an SNTP request immediately at startup. After a successful
    correction it sleeps cooperatively for one day. Failed attempts retry after
    one minute, five minutes, thirty minutes, then hourly. It is intended to run
    under the SCFG service supervisor.

    The initial example targets the QEMU gateway at 10.0.2.2. The application
    validates an SNTPv4 server reply, echoed originate token, stratum, source,
    and nonzero timestamps. It supports NTP era zero through 2036 and requires
    datagram, monotonic timer, and privileged clock-control authority.
